bank={x['id']:x for x in json.loads((R/'build/work/mcq/9702.tagged.json').read_text())}
ids=['9702_w24_13_q31','9702_w23_13_q30','9702_w23_12_q30','9702_s23_12_q30','9702_s19_11_q32','9702_s19_12_q33','9702_w21_13_q33','9702_w21_12_q33','9702_s22_13_q32','9702_s21_13_q33','9702_w23_11_q30','9702_w24_13_q32']
ex=['Current is a flow of charge carriers. B confuses current with energy transfer.','Neutrons have no charge; protons and alpha- and beta-particles are charged.','Only B is not an integer multiple of $e=1.60\\times10^{-19}$ C; zero is $0e$ and is possible.','Only C equals an integer multiple, $3e$; B is $2.5e$.','D is $2.5e$, which is impossible. A is $-3e$ and the negative sign does not make it impossible.','At steady current, equal charge passes both sections in the same time. A wrongly changes charge with area.','Total charge is $10^{20}e=16$ C; $I=Q/t=16/(30\\times10^{-6})\\approx 5.3\\times10^5$ A, so D. C misses a factor of 1000.','One coulomb is the charge transferred by 1 A in 1 s. A is only one elementary charge.','The series current is equal; doubling diameter quadruples area, so the speed ratio $v_X/v_Y=4$. A reverses the ratio.','Use $nA=N/L$, so $I=Nqv/L=0.27$ A. B multiplies by the wire length instead of dividing.','Number density is carriers per unit volume. B incorrectly says per unit area.','New area is $0.25A$ and new speed is $3v$, so current is $0.75I$. B treats area as proportional to diameter.']
